/* Stall watchdog, armed only while streaming.
 *
 * When the device stops responding it does so silently: no assert, no fault,
 * nothing on the console, and the network simply goes quiet. NuttX only dumps
 * task state when something crashes, so a hang leaves no evidence at all --
 * which is why it has stayed undiagnosed.
 *
 * This manufactures the evidence. The stream is the device's most regular
 * activity, so if it stops making progress for this long something is stuck;
 * the watchdog fires from the timer interrupt, which runs whatever else the
 * system is doing, and panics deliberately to get the full task dump.
 *
 * Bring-up instrumentation -- remove when the hang is understood.
 */

#define MIC_STALL_DUMP_S 15

